\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8c3dbf252eff53944dac86aa413567518b95718f5ee98d0da9f2caadf8d4b8bc","event_uuid":"689463ed-ea8a-4826-9d25-5b65310f649c","position":{"commit_sha":"baf8cc1d5776a55b116d95688af994b1f17ce333","position":"1787392132862640001-689463ed-ea8a-4826-9d25-5b65310f649c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b2643231363777e431eea275284789ba26e04a81aa5914a575fe2a6d83aa3b6a","event_uuid":"306162f1-1135-433a-8258-5807351adab5","position":{"commit_sha":"39917cb7a00b22f59747a28773719671b981209d","position":"1787392143644426001-306162f1-1135-433a-8258-5807351adab5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-239_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"e50ec61e-3a77-4eb8-b56b-c1d0f90ff9bc","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan rewritten after verifying every claim in the original description against the tree (commit 960fbfef2f).\n\nClaims found FALSE and removed:\n- `build_usage_limits` returning the bare `req_limit` was described as a drift bug. It is deliberate and documented at structured_run.py:427-432 (RP-01 S2): telemetry and `completion_banking.iteration_limit_for`'s 2*B inverse both read the bare base; the output-retry allowance is an addend only inside the constructed UsageLimits. Making it allowance-inclusive would BREAK both readers. The old AC `iteration_limit_for(build_usage_limits(...))` was also not type-correct — build_usage_limits returns a 3-tuple.\n- `completion_recovery.py:307`, `passes.py:388` and `fidelity_spot_eval.py:103,115` were listed as single-turn sites. All four are `execution_mode=\"agentic\"`. `passes.py:520` is single_turn but `mode=\"text\"`, so it is not part of the structured construct either.\n- `code_review/workflow_ops.py:604` — the RunRequest is at :612.\n- `workflow/interpreter.py` was in the guard allowlist as a direct RunRequest site; it constructs `BatchRunRequest`, a different class.\n- The site list omitted two real single-turn structured sites: `evals/eval_solver.py:167` and `plan_review/__init__.py:172`.\n- AC1 asked that judge_one and judge_batch declare the same bound set. `kaolinite-head-wildebeest` (3939) closed exactly that as not_a_bug: judge_one has no production caller. Bounding it is out of scope now; it gets an explicit `bounds=RunRequest.INHERIT_POLICY` (behaviour unchanged).\n- A required `model_class` argument was dropped: several adopting sites deliberately inherit `cfg.model`, so forcing a class would change which model they call — a behaviour change, and bug afeb's mechanism already owns that question.\n- `iteration_limit` dropped from the builder: a single_turn run has `tools=[]` and `req_limit = max(1, ...)`, so it is a no-op there.\n\nClaim found TRUE and kept: only judge_batch declares the four lowering-only seams, and only completion_recovery.py:413 sets a token cap — verified by grep over src/rebar.\n\nNew scope item the original plan missed: `tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py::_run_request_sites` matches only `node.func.id == \"RunRequest\"`. Adopting a classmethod makes fourteen sites invisible to it, so the oracle would FAIL OPEN while its frozen 24-entry table assertion fails. The fix is three lines in the matcher; the table's keys, config expressions and verdicts are untouched.\n\nLine accounting: the original plan implied net-negative. Honest estimate is about line-neutral — the description says so rather than claiming otherwise.","timestamp":1787377569113547001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC EVIDENCE, verified against merged main (Gerrit 2084, commit f4f35f7bfa).\n\nAC1 uniqueness guard: tests/unit/test_run_request_builder.py::test_the_single_turn_structured_request_is_built_only_by_for_structured passes. The guard is self-testing - test_the_guard_catches_a_hand_built_site_and_a_reasoned_marker_excuses_it writes a synthetic hand-built site, confirms the guard FIRES, confirms a reasoned '# single-turn-structured-ok: vendored' marker EXCUSES it, and confirms a BARE reasonless marker still fires. That is the three-way mutation proof done in-test rather than by hand.\nAC2 builder edge cases: same suite, 6 passed - for_structured without bounds and SingleTurnBounds with any field missing both raise TypeError.\nAC3 site table: tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py, 13 passed - _EXPECTED_RUN_REQUEST_SITES still lists all 24 sites with the same keys, config expressions and verdicts after adoption.\n\nAC4 no assertion edits - HOLDS, with a nuance worth recording rather than ticking blindly. The landed tests/ delta is +25/-0, +194/-0, and +37/-4. The four deletions are all in test_subcall_class_selection.py's AST-scanning HELPER (calls_by_name, _ast_index(), a docstring, and a 'node.func.id != RunRequest' check), teaching the scanner to recognise RunRequest.for_structured(...) alongside RunRequest(...). No assertion was touched, and AC3 independently confirms the scanner still finds the same 24 sites with the same verdicts.\n\nSeparately fixed during review (recorded on the change): the RP-01 census in test_rp01_s5_authoritative_oracle.py asserts >=10 files construct structured requests, as a proxy for the census MECHANISM resolving computed and multi-line modes. It only recognised RunRequest(mode=...), so consolidating fourteen hand-built sites dropped it to 4 and failed on all four CI shards - it was measuring the SPELLING, not the property. Taught _scope_constructs_structured that reaching the builder is itself proof of a structured construction; the census now sees 11 files, so the >=10 threshold was left alone rather than lowered to fit.","timestamp":1787390853942255001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787352354398276001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"e60082d9-adde-4982-8818-bb1977c26e47","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b2c1-53d3-e838-4e12"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nFourteen call sites in `src/rebar/llm` hand-build the SAME single-turn structured request\nshape: `mode=\"structured\"` + `output_schema=<name>` + `execution_mode=\"single_turn\"`, with\n`system_prompt` / `instructions` / `config` / `reviewers`. Verified on the tree:\n`overlap/judge.py:163,203`, `enrich.py:183`, `epic_bug_screen.py:266`,\n`evals/eval_solver.py:167`, `plan_review/__init__.py:172`, `plan_review/prerequisites.py:231`,\n`plan_review/xcheck.py:199,337`, `plan_review/completion_subcall.py:193`,\n`plan_review/passes.py:469,582`, `workflow/completion_recovery.py:404`,\n`code_review/workflow_ops.py:612`.\n\nTwo consequences of the copy-paste:\n\n1. `RunRequest`'s own contract (`runner.py:96-100`) says a `single_turn` request must also carry\n   `mode=\"structured\"` + `output_schema` \"so the two stay consistent\" — but nothing enforces it;\n   it is re-asserted by hand fourteen times.\n2. The bounding decision is invisible. Only ONE of the fourteen declares any of the four\n   lowering-only seams (`output_token_limit` / `structured_retry_limit` /\n   `transport_attempt_limit` / `request_timeout_limit_s`): `judge_batch` (judge.py:211-214), and\n   only `completion_recovery.py:413` sets a token cap. Confirmed by\n   `grep -rn \"output_token_limit=\\|structured_retry_limit=\\|transport_attempt_limit=\\|request_timeout_limit_s=\" src/rebar`.\n   Omission is silent, so an unbounded site reads exactly like a deliberately-unbounded one.\n   That is the shape of bug `leathery-druidic-nurseshark` (22da): it bounded `judge_batch` and\n   the identical `judge_one` block four lines up stayed unbounded, unnoticed for days.\n\nNot in scope, deliberately:\n- **Bounding any site.** Every site keeps its CURRENT effective bounds. In particular\n  `judge_one` stays unbounded: `kaolinite-head-wildebeest` (3939) closed `not_a_bug` on the\n  grounds that `judge_one` has no production caller, and this story does not reopen it.\n- **Model-class binding.** That is bug `afeb`'s mechanism (`cfg = replace(cfg, model=...)`)\n  with its own oracle in `tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py`; folding a `model_class`\n  argument into the builder would CHANGE the model at the sites that deliberately inherit.\n- **`build_usage_limits` / `iteration_limit_for`.** `build_usage_limits` returning the BARE\n  `req_limit` is deliberate and documented (`structured_run.py:427-432`, RP-01 S2): telemetry\n  and `completion_banking.iteration_limit_for`'s `2*B` inverse both read the bare base, and the\n  retry allowance is an addend only inside the constructed `UsageLimits`. There is no drift to\n  fix. A single-turn run makes one model call with `tools=[]`, so `iteration_limit` is a no-op\n  for it and the builder does not expose it.\n\n## Approach\nOne shared constructor for the shape; the bounds decision becomes a REQUIRED argument.\n\n1. `structured_run.py` (leaf module): add a frozen dataclass `SingleTurnBounds` with four\n   fields and **no defaults** — `output_tokens`, `timeout_s`, `structured_retries`,\n   `transport_attempts`, each `int | None`. `None` means \"inherit run-wide policy\", which is\n   what an omitted seam does today (every seam is lowering-only: `runner._effective_config`\n   `min()`s timeout/transport, `structured_run.output_retry_allowance` `min()`s retries).\n2. `runner.py`: add `RunRequest.for_structured(*, system_prompt, instructions, config,\n   reviewers, output_schema, bounds, target=None)` — keyword-only, `bounds` required — which\n   fixes `mode=\"structured\"` and `execution_mode=\"single_turn\"` and maps `bounds` onto the four\n   `RunRequest` fields. Add `RunRequest.INHERIT_POLICY: ClassVar[SingleTurnBounds]`, the named\n   all-`None` value, so a site that inherits says so in one greppable token and needs no new\n   import.\n3. Adopt at all fourteen sites. Thirteen pass `bounds=RunRequest.INHERIT_POLICY`; `judge_batch`\n   passes its existing four values; `completion_recovery.py:404` passes its token cap with the\n   other three `None`. Byte-identical resulting `RunRequest` at every site.\n4. Extend the existing site oracle. `tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py::_run_request_sites`\n   matches only `node.func.id == \"RunRequest\"`, so after adoption it would stop seeing fourteen\n   sites and FAIL OPEN. Teach it to accept `RunRequest.for_structured` as well. The frozen\n   `_EXPECTED_RUN_REQUEST_SITES` table (24 entries, its keys, config expressions and verdicts)\n   is UNCHANGED — the `config=` expression at each site is untouched — so this is an\n   oracle-scope repair, not an assertion edit.\n\n## Guard construction\nPer the parent epic `airborne-wellloved-kingfisher`: owner module (`runner.py`) exempt; match\nthe AST conjunction that constitutes the construct — a direct `RunRequest(...)` call carrying\nBOTH `execution_mode=\"single_turn\"` and `mode=\"structured\"` — never a single token; escape\nmarker `# single-turn-structured-ok: <reason>` with a mandatory non-empty reason, as\n`scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py` uses; behaviour pinned only by the named existing tests.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/llm/runner.py`, `src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py`, the fourteen call sites above,\n`tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py` (oracle scope only),\n`tests/unit/test_run_request_builder.py` (new).\n\nLine delta: adoption removes one line per site (two keywords out, one `bounds=` in); the shared\nbuilder plus dataclass add roughly thirty. This child is about line-neutral, not net-negative;\nthe epic's net-negative criterion is a SUM over its consolidation children.\n\n## Testing\n- Builder unit tests: `for_structured` returns `mode=\"structured\"` /\n  `execution_mode=\"single_turn\"`; each `SingleTurnBounds` field lands on its `RunRequest` field;\n  `INHERIT_POLICY` leaves all four `None`.\n- Edge: `for_structured(...)` without `bounds` raises `TypeError`; `SingleTurnBounds(...)`\n  missing any field raises `TypeError`.\n- Guard test (AST, `src/rebar` minus `runner.py`) with a marker-honouring escape and a test\n  that an unreasoned marker does not excuse a site.\n- Pinning, unchanged assertions: `tests/unit/test_overlap_judge.py`,\n  `tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py` (site table), `tests/unit/test_enrich.py`,\n  `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_banking.py`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] No file under `src/rebar` except `runner.py` constructs a `RunRequest` carrying both\n      `execution_mode=\"single_turn\"` and `mode=\"structured\"` without a reasoned\n      `# single-turn-structured-ok:` marker; checked by the new guard test.\n- [x] Calling `RunRequest.for_structured` without `bounds`, and `SingleTurnBounds` with any\n      field missing, both raise `TypeError`; checked by the builder edge tests.\n- [x] `_EXPECTED_RUN_REQUEST_SITES` still lists all 24 sites with the same keys, config\n      expressions and verdicts after adoption; checked by\n      `pytest tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py`.\n- [x] The pinning suites above pass with no assertion edits; checked by `pytest`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner.py","reason":"RunRequest.for_structured builder + INHERIT_POLICY"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py","reason":"SingleTurnBounds dataclass"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/overlap/judge.py","reason":"adopt builder (judge_one, judge_batch)"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/enrich.py","reason":"adopt builder"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/epic_bug_screen.py","reason":"adopt builder"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/eval_solver.py","reason":"adopt builder"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py","reason":"adopt builder"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/prerequisites.py","reason":"adopt builder"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/xcheck.py","reason":"adopt builder"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/completion_subcall.py","reason":"adopt builder"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py","reason":"adopt builder"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py","reason":"adopt builder"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py","reason":"adopt builder"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_run_request_builder.py","reason":"new builder + uniqueness guard tests"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_subcall_class_selection.py","reason":"site oracle must also see for_structured calls"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a"],["relates_to","b2c1-53d3-e838-4e12"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","parent_status_uuid":"689463ed-ea8a-4826-9d25-5b65310f649c","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["consolidation","janitor","fortnight-review"],"ticket_id":"44ff-2ad0-e994-4da7","ticket_type":"story","title":"RunRequest.for_structured builder with required bounds for single-turn LLM calls","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["82a3e652-9680-4440-9c67-32d34c5dfe69","cf04623a-0fef-4914-a1f2-aef847623a5e","e7dbfeaa-23e7-4a44-b8f9-609c0b53908f","dda7b14a-63ad-4c5f-95d5-1b734fdd4534","0921a960-8601-4c49-bf8a-b74f917cded6","27a99dcf-769c-4e5e-916b-dd684b316798","e317fb38-0bf8-4b28-95d5-040078d07c6a","e60082d9-adde-4982-8818-bb1977c26e47","8f720568-0728-4180-a35e-0e6c1ee488d8","b99de5c2-8904-4edd-a538-29965a9ef369","689463ed-ea8a-4826-9d25-5b65310f649c","306162f1-1135-433a-8258-5807351adab5"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787400234460445001,"uuid":"8e975287-c5a5-4e12-bb08-790847d58678"}